4. The mathematics of hunting

For independent attempts with probability per attempt, the chance of at least one success after trials is:

P(\text{at least one success})=1-(1-p)^n

At base modern shiny odds of 1 in 4,096, performing 4,096 independent encounters does not mean a shiny is guaranteed. It means approximately a 63.2% cumulative probability of at least one shiny.

Likewise, failing 4,095 times doesn’t make your next independent attempt more likely. ShinyHunt +1

